(`m's values` gives a list of its own: a list or map value is copied, as
 every read-out of a collection is, so freeing that list (which frees the
 collections it holds) leaves the map whole.)
a map called shelf is {"fruit": ["apple"], "meta": {"n": 1}}.
a list called vals is shelf's values.
Free vals.
Print "shelf: {shelf}".
a list called again is shelf's values.
Print "again: {again}".
